[{:db/id 17592186203686 :question/problem "|  | $\\bigstar$ | $\\maltese$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $4$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $5$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nThe adjacency matrix of the relation $R,$ defined over the sets $\\{ 3, 4, 5 \\}$ and $\\{ \\bigstar, \\maltese \\},$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(4, \\bigstar)$\n\nII. $(5, \\maltese)$\n\nIII. $(3, \\maltese)$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186413693 :question/problem "Consider the following relation on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1)}\n$$\n\nWhat are the domain and range of this relation?\n\nThe domain is \n${x\\in $\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,:\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$}$\n\nThe range is {{field-3}}" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204264 :question/problem "Consider the following relation on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y={e}^{x}}\n$$\n\nWhat are the domain and range of this relation?\n\nThe domain is {{field-1}}\n\nThe range is {{field-2}}" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186413694 :question/problem "|  | $✠$ | $♣$ | $♠$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $✠$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $♣$ | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $♠$ | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nThe adjacency matrix of the relation $R,$ defined on the set ${✠,♣,♠},$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(✠,♣)$\n\nII. $(♣,♠)$\n\nIII. $(♠,✠)$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186413696 :question/problem "|  | $3$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $4$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $8$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nThe adjacency matrix of the relation $R,$ defined over the sets ${2,4,8}$ and ${3,6},$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\nI. $(4,3)$\n\nII. $(8,6)$\n\nIII. $(2,3)$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
